  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen Central Asian Media in Climate Action and Disaster Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO Almaty will strengthen media institutions in Central Asia, an arid, landlocked and snow-fed region that is particularly vulnerable to climate change and disasters, so that they can have a greater impact on climate action and disaster preparedness and response in the region, by providing essential information, facilitating public debates, holding powerful actors accountable, uncovering disaster risks, and promoting solutions to challenges across national borders.

Through a combination of funding sources, UNESCO Almaty will also seek to support Central Asian states and media stakeholders to create an enabling environment for the development of free, independent, and pluralistic media, including community media. In addition, it will implement media development projects that enhance media pluralism and viability and improve the diversity of media organizations and editorial content.</narrative>
  </description>
